Upstream MIT preservation (Deep Code)
--------------------------------------
DeepOrca derives from Deep Code (https://github.com/lessweb/deepcode-cli),
originally licensed under the MIT License by lessweb. The repository's root
commit `a791317` (2026-04-28) is the import of deepcode-cli v0.1.1 (52 files).

A provenance audit (2026-08-19; line-level best-match of the upstream sources
against the current tree) established:

- No upstream file survives verbatim; the upstream CLI and terminal UI were
  fully replaced (zero overlap).
- Roughly 2,000 substantive lines of the engine are inherited/adapted from
  upstream code, concentrated in `packages/core/src`:
  `session.ts` (session loop), `tools/edit-handler.ts`, `tools/read-handler.ts`,
  `tools/bash-handler.ts`, `tools/write-handler.ts`,
  `tools/ask-user-question-handler.ts`, `tools/web-search-handler.ts`,
  `tools/executor.ts`, `prompt.ts`, `settings.ts`, `common/file-utils.ts`,
  `common/state.ts`, `common/notify.ts`.
- Everything else (desktop GUI, memory/embedding packages, routing, actions,
  MCP extensions, docs, specs) is authored by the DeepOrca project.

